System Integration and Communication

All active components (ball, pitch, boots, vest) are nodes on a stadium‑wide private 5G‑URLLC network with <5 ms end‑to‑end latency and 99.9999% reliability. Time synchronisation uses IEEE 802.1AS PTP (jitter <1 μs).

Key data flows:

· Boot → Pitch Grid: Phase classification + foot trajectory prediction (50 Hz).
· Pitch Grid → Vest: Plant trigger + desired counter‑torque (command issued 10 ms pre‑contact).
· Ball → Pitch Grid: State vector, restitution mode, CMG health (100 Hz).
· Pitch Grid → Referee HUD: All infraction events, telemetry warnings.

