Verification Principle

The entire system is considered compliant if, during a full‑match simulation, the following hold simultaneously:

· Ball‑foot touch interval distribution matches Earth reference to within 5 ms RMS.
· Plant‑foot lateral force impulse during cuts matches Earth baseline within 10%.
· No overturning torso events occur that exceed the IEV’s 200 ms recovery window.
· The ball’s in‑flight curvature for a given spin vector and speed falls within 5% of Earth‑equivalent trajectory.

The Dribble Preservation Standard is met when the game feels fast, close, and rhythmically identical to the sport played on Earth — even though the physics of the planet have changed entirely.


